course: dictionary
lesson: 9869
title: Short words, friendly meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some short words are informal, which means people use them in relaxed, friendly talk, not in formal writing. «Ta» is one of these. When someone hands you a biscuit and you hear «Ta, mate», the clues show it is a thank you.
explain: The word «ta» is mostly used in Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand. Context helps again: if a friend says «Ta very much» after you help carry their bag, you know they are thankful.
explain: Look out for «ta-ta». It is informal British English and means goodbye, often said to small children. The word «ta» can also be part of longer words, so always check the whole word before you decide what it means.
fact: «Ta» is an informal interjection, so it is a short word people say to show a feeling.
fact: In Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, «ta» means «thank you».
fact: «Ta very much» is a slightly stronger way of saying thank you.
fact: «Ta-ta» is an informal British word that means goodbye, often said to small children.
fact: A TA is short for teaching assistant, a helper who works with the teacher in school. In French, «ta» means «your», but that is a different word.
exercise: Jake mumbles «ta» after you pass him the pen. What does he mean? | Sorry, I am late | Goodbye for ever | Please come here | *Thank you
exercise: «Ta-ta, see you tomorrow!» What does ta-ta mean? | *Goodbye | Hello | Be quiet | Thank you very much
exercise: In a school, the TA helps the teacher with the reading group. What does TA stand for? | Tall adult | Team activity | Test answer | *Teaching assistant
test: «Ta, mate» is used in which places? | Only in French schools | In every country in the world | Only in the USA | *Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand
test: Ben says «ta-ta» to his little sister at the door. What does he mean? | *Goodbye | Stop shouting | Good morning | Thank you for the drink
exam: Which word means «thank you» in an informal way, as in «Ta, mate»? | *Ta | Ta-ta | Mate | TA
